```

This ensures non-Claude models (OpenAI) interleave charts with explanatory text by:
1. Making the constraint explicit in the system prompt
2. Including a `next_step` directive in each chart result
3. Using hard-constraint language ("FORBIDDEN", "MUST") that resonates with non-Claude models

### **Per-Request Abort Tracking (lines 37-40)**

The sidecar tracks active request IDs to support cancellation:
```typescript
const activeAborts = new Map<number, AbortController>();

// Client disconnect detection
res.on("close", () => {
  if (!responseEnded) {
    abortController.abort();
  }
});
```

The `/stop` endpoint (lines 394-404) allows graceful termination of all active agents.

